+# Marginalia Books
+
+A static website for Marginalia Books, a fictional independent bookshop. It has four pages:
+the home page, a catalogue of books with a genre filter, a list of upcoming and past events,
+and a visit page with opening hours, the address and a contact form. Every title, author and
+event is invented.
+
+The site is plain HTML, CSS and JavaScript. There is no build step and no dependencies, and
+it makes no requests beyond its own files.
+
+## Viewing the site
+
+Either open `index.html` directly in a browser, or serve the folder with any static server:
+
+```sh
+python3 -m http.server 8000
+```
+
+Then open http://localhost:8000/.
+
+## Files
+
+- `index.html`, `books.html`, `events.html`, `visit.html`: the four pages.
+- `css/styles.css`: the shared stylesheet for every page.
+- `js/books-data.js`: the catalogue, as a JavaScript array on `window.BOOKS`.
+- `js/books.js`: builds the genre filter and book cards, and keeps the genre in `?genre=`.
+- `js/events-data.js`: the events, as a JavaScript array on `window.EVENTS`.
+- `js/events.js`: sorts events into upcoming and past using the visitor's local date.
+- `js/contact.js`: validation for the demo contact form on the visit page.
+- `favicon.svg`: the site icon.
+- `tests/`: the browser tests (see below).
+
+Data is kept in plain script files, not fetched, so the pages also work from `file://`.
+
+## Running the tests
+
+The tests drive the system Chrome through the globally installed Playwright, and start their
+own static server from `tests/server.js`.
+
+```sh
+NODE_PATH=$(npm root -g) node --test tests/*.test.js
+```
+
+Set `PLAYWRIGHT_CHROME` to use a different Chrome binary. The default is `/usr/bin/google-chrome`.
